bin/
dist/

# `go build ./` inside a main package's own directory drops the binary beside the source, named after
# that directory — so the three tools whose main sits in cmd/ drop a file called `cmd`, not the tool
# name. bin/ and dist/ cover neither. Left untracked, a `git add -A` in any session commits a ~3MB
# binary. gitignore cannot say "a file named after its directory", so this list is written out, and
# gitignore_test.go is what notices when a tool is added and this list is not.
**/cmd/cmd
/cite-graph/cite-graph
/go-mutate/go-mutate
/rule-echo/rule-echo
